	{/* ── The copyright footer (2026-08-10, Hiro: add a footer) ──
	    Lifted verbatim from the home page, exactly as the about page's was
	    (08-05) and for the same reason: same element, same max-w-[960px]/px-5
	    so the line sits on the SAME left edge as the prose, the h2 above it and
	    the leftmost strip card's year, same py-10, same text-xs on --ink-soft.
	    A copyright line is the lowest-priority text on the site and the home
	    page settled what that looks like; a third treatment would be a third
	    answer to a solved question. All three routes now end the same way.

	    OUTSIDE <main>, matching both. It isn't page content and the reveal
	    cascade doesn't touch it — no .reveal, no --i, so it is simply there
	    when the page is.

	    NOTE this replaces a footer that was a BACK LINK rather than a
	    copyright, and about.astro's footer note used to cite that difference as
	    the reason it took the home page's version instead. That distinction is
	    gone: there is one footer on the site now, in three places. The note
	    over there has been corrected.

	    ── What the old footer was, and what removing it took with it ──
	    It held exactly one thing: a "Back to projects" link whose slug sent you
	    to the CARD you came from, at the scroll position you left it. It was the
